          "source": "thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "This is a smooth future unit timelike Born-rigid congruence. If $\\Omega\\ne0$, its three-dimensional rest distribution in the ambient open set is nowhere integrable: its vorticity is nowhere zero and no ambient rest-simultaneity hypersurface exists locally. If $\\Omega=0$, $n=\\partial_0$ is inertial and irrotational, and the rest hypersurfaces are $x^0=const$. Now fix $R>0$ with $|\\Omega|R<c$ and restrict to the timelike ring cylinder $r=R$, $x^3=const$, whose rotating angle is $\\varphi=\\phi-\\Omega t$ modulo $2\\pi$, with $x^0=ct$. The ring observer $\\phi=\\phi_0+\\Omega t$ has $n=\\gamma(R)\\bigl(1,-(\\Omega R/c)\\sin\\phi,(\\Omega R/c)\\cos\\phi,0\\bigr)$. The induced metric is $-(c^2-\\Omega^2R^2)dt^2+2\\Omega R^2\\,dt\\,d\\varphi+R^2d\\varphi^2$. The ambient rest covector restricted to the cylinder is proportional to $-(c^2-\\Omega^2R^2)dt+\\Omega R^2d\\varphi$, so the one-dimensional rest distribution on that cylinder is locally integrable and satisfies $dt/d\\varphi=\\Omega R^2/(c^2-\\Omega^2R^2)$. After one positive circuit in the rotating label, its lift starting at $t=0$ has signed time offset $\\Delta t=2\\pi\\Omega R^2/(c^2-\\Omega^2R^2)$. For $\\Omega\\ne0$ it returns to the same rotating label at a different time and does not close as a ring rest-simultaneity curve; there is no globally single-valued real rest-synchronization time on the entire cylinder with time-oriented nonzero differential annihilating these rest lines. This global ring holonomy is distinct from the ambient local Frobenius obstruction. For $\\Omega=0$ the offset is zero and ring rest lines are $t=const$.",
