          "claim": "(The segment and the crossing.) With $p=x^{-1}(-1,0,0,0)$, $q=x^{-1}(3,1,0,0)$ and $y(s)=p+s(q-p)$, the tangent is the constant displacement $(4,1,0,0)$ by [L2] and [L3]; its $\\eta$-square is $-16+1=-15<0$ with time component $4>0$, so every tangent is future timelike by [L1] and $y$ is a future timelike curve; the coordinate $x^0-x^1$ equals $-1+3s$ along $y$, which is $-1$ at $s=0$, $2$ at $s=1$, and vanishes exactly at $s=1/3$, giving the crossing event $x^{-1}(1/3,1/3,0,0)\\in H$.",
